Lobium — native language and configured-geolocation consumers.

NavigatorLanguage is shared by Window Navigator and every WorkerNavigator, including service workers,
so one hook makes language/languages identical in all contexts. Accept-Language remains sourced from the
pre-start profile preference written by the launcher (Chromium's canonical network-context path);
Intl locale uses --lang and timezone uses inherited TZ, both process-wide.

Configured geolocation replaces the provider's coordinates only after Chromium's normal secure-context
and permission flow succeeds. This preserves real permission semantics while preventing the host
location from leaking once access is granted.

The renderer applies locale.locale to ICU before Blink/V8 initialization, so default Intl locale is
identical even when Chromium's UI resource pack only has a language-level locale (for example `de`).

